From 0de5e4a9e70d45859229b1eb7d781b44dacd0336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Batchelor <srbatchelor@ovgl.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:21:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] EnclaveConnectivity v2: the provider-routed mode is named
 for providers, not TUNA

Pure renames; storage layout, checks and arithmetic are unchanged:
- Host.tuna -> Host.provider (setHost, capabilities, capabilitiesFor, HostConfigured)
- viaTuna -> viaProviders, _tunaProviders -> _providers, tunaProviders -> providersOf,
  TunaAuthorized -> ProvidersAuthorized
- tunaPolicyDigest -> providerPolicyDigest (domain "EnclaveConnectivity.provider-policy.v1"),
  authorizeTuna -> authorizeProviders, quoteTuna -> quoteProvider
- TunaReceipt -> ProviderReceipt, tunaReceiptDigest -> providerReceiptDigest
  (domain "EnclaveConnectivity.provider-receipt.v1"), settleTuna -> settleProvider

ABI and site/js/gen/contract-artifacts.js regenerated (scripts/build-contract-artifacts.mjs;
the ABI equals solc 0.8.35 --via-ir runs 200 output). Foundry suite renamed: 26/26 pass.
Not deployed: the live ledger's bandwidthRouter is one-time bound to v1 (0x5f8b636e).

Co-Authored-By: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
