From f4a357c0e9a61b12aa0bef4393e8c76eb3a2b126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Batchelor <srbatchelor@ovgl.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:21:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] network, relay, site, scripts: callers use the
 EnclaveConnectivity v2 provider-mode names

- lease snapshot (connectivity-chain.mjs): viaProviders / providersOf reads; the snapshot fields
  are connectivity.viaProviders and connectivity.providerMode (were viaTuna / tunaProvider);
  consumers (provider-settlement, usdc-bandwidth, paid-fork-e2e, tests) follow
- provider-settlement: settleProvider, receipt domain "EnclaveConnectivity.provider-receipt.v1"
- onchain-qualification: hosts()/setHost() field named provider
- relay/vaultsvc.js: the bandwidth mode 'tuna' is now 'providers' (providerPolicyDigest /
  authorizeProviders); "providers require provider authorization"; networkArgs gets a unit test
- site Network tab: providerPolicyDigest 5c50050e / authorizeProviders 2be89fe4 calldata,
  mode "providers"; its test now encodes against contracts/EnclaveConnectivity.abi.json
- scripts/network/connectivity.mjs: command and --mode value 'providers'
- scripts/network/paid-fork-e2e.mjs: when the fork's ledger is bound to a contract without the
  v2 interface (today: production v1), or with --fresh, the fork's one-time bandwidthRouter slot
  is cleared and a fresh contract from --artifact is bound (fork only)
- comments say provider / Enclave network instead of TUNA

These callers need a v2 contract: against the deployed v1 (0x5f8b636e) the renamed reads revert.

Co-Authored-By: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
